# Prject Description
This project analyzes customer sign up behavior and evaluates data quality for Rapid Scale, a fast growing SaaS company with tiered 
subscription plans. The work supports the Monthly Business Review by providing reliable insights into how users join the platform, 
which plans they choose, and where data issues may affect reporting and decisions.

The project focuses on auditing a recent customer sign up dataset to identify inaccuracies, inconsistencies, and missing information. 
You clean and standardize the data to ensure it is fit for analysis. This includes correcting inconsistent category values, handling 
missing fields, removing duplicates, and enforcing correct data types. The outcome is a trusted dataset that can be used confidently 
by the Business Intelligence, Marketing, and Onboarding teams.

After cleaning, the project produces clear summary metrics that describe user acquisition trends. These summaries show how sign ups 
change over time, which marketing sources and regions drive growth, how customers select subscription plans, and how marketing opt in 
behavior varies across demographics. Age based analysis highlights differences in plan preference and engagement patterns.

The project also answers practical business questions that directly support decision making. You identify the most effective acquisition 
channels, highlight regions with data quality gaps, assess whether age influences marketing opt in, and determine which plans attract 
different age groups. An optional extension links customer sign ups with support ticket data to understand early customer support needs 
by plan and region.

Deliverables include a Jupyter Notebook that documents the full analysis workflow and a concise PDF report that explains findings in 
business language. Together, they demonstrate your ability to manage the full data analysis lifecycle. From raw data quality assessment 
to actionable insights that inform marketing and onboarding strategy.
